※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4508

※ Three of the four roundings say which way they go, and two of one with the
※ same value answer alike wherever the program runs.  The fourth asks the
※ processor what it is doing just now, which is state outside the function and
※ outside the language -- so a function that writes it is not pure, and says so
※ with `@[impure]`.

fn rounded(x: f64) → f64:
    ⇕x

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕ord('a')
    0u6
